  "details": "The current Avatars menu is inconsistent and frustrating to use.\n\n- Sorting avatars by \"date added\" sorts them by their original upload date, which is rarely relevant to users.\n\n- Sorting worlds by \"date added\" sorts them by the date they were added to your favorites, which is much more practical, but adds confusion as to what \"date added\" is supposed to mean.\n\n- On the website, both avatars and worlds can be sorted by \"favorite added\"\n\nThis creates a confusing and disjointed user experience. \n\nMost players want to quickly access their recently favorited avatars, not the ones uploaded to the platform most recently - especially since the in-game UI doesn’t even show the original date of upload (only the most recent update). To view the original upload date, users have to go to the website, which makes the current sorting even less helpful, and it makes the in-game sorting seem random (you can find multiple bug reports about this).\n\nSuggested improvements:\n\n- Rename the avatar's \"date added\" to \"upload date\" if it really needs to remain available.\n\n- Add a new sorting option for avatars: \"favorite added\" (or \"date favorited\")\n\n- Rename the \"date added\" option in the Favorite Worlds tab to \"favorite added\" (or \"date favorited\") for consistency across the UI",
